WEBVTT

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.250
"10 YEARS AGO"

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.080
What?

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.080
What do you mean you have to go
to another country again?

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.830
It's my job.
I have to do my job, right?

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.870
We know you might get lonely,
but just hang in there.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.950
B-But...

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.750
The maids will take care of everything
while we're gone.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.370
It's all right.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.700
Mom.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.120
Grandma Sakura!

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.120
While you're gone, just leave everything
to me and little Sakura.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.580
Thank you for helping with her.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.950
Grandma's here, so everything will be fine!

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.370
I love you, Grandma!

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.870
"The Promised Flower"

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.370
So you really did get
an invitation like this, huh?

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.660
Well, you seemed like you were
really trying to hide all of it.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.660
There was no way to tell you
I was going to your concert.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.160
But I was surprised
you were an idol this whole time.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.250
Right?

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.870
Are you okay?

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.160
Not overdoing it, are you?

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.870
It's so odd.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.700
Even though that was our first performance,

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.870
and I'm really uncomfortable
standing in front of people and smiling...

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:14.200
I have this feeling now that I can do
so much more than before.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.500
Lunch?

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.200
You're going to be late
standing around like that.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.620
Now get going!

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.580
Wait, Mom...

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.290
Have a good day.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.040
Thank you.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:43.200
But still, who sent that letter?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.830
A letter? To your house?

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.290
I have no clue.
No one told me about that.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.200
I-Is that so?

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:56.410
If Mr. Gouda didn't send it, who did?

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.620
Was it the Wall?

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.540
What is the Wall, exactly?

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.790
Hi, Father. Just checking in.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.910
Me?

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:16.750
I made new friends. Uh-huh.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.750
Dang, she's totally fluent!

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.790
Of course she is. She was born and raised
in the country of freedom.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:25.370
She's bright, positive, and honest.
Three things you want in a beautiful girl.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.160
Her parents raised her well.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.000
She's a goddess of freedom!

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.160
Yeah!

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.160
And you're a goddess of idiocy.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.830
That's right, and I can't read
the Declaration of Independence, either.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.040
No. I don't even know how I survived.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.830
What do you mean by that?

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.040
I'm jealous.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.540
She keeps going on and on
without a care in the world.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.330
--Like you're one to talk.
--Like you're one to talk.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.450
Are you gonna come anytime soon?

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:52.950
A-Again?

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:55.290
I can't stand this sound!

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.370
Here it comes!

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.790
"SUCCESSFULLY COMPLETE A PHOTO SHOOT
AT HITOME SENBONZAKURA"

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.660
As you may have heard,
we'll be heading to Nara.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.830
Are y'all kidding? That's a fast plot twist!

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:10.660
Yay!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.450
Reindeer! Reindeer!

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.910
You mean a regular deer?

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.290
Our negotiations with the publisher
were last minute,

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.910
so you will appear on next month's cover
of "Weekly Shonen Monday Magazine."

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.330
A cover?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.620
Everyone, please get ready to leave.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:33.410
Another sudden notice!
I don't even know what to pack.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:34.910
Rice crackers for deer!

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:37.580
You can pick some up when we get there.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.750
It'll take two and a half hours by bullet train.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.750
Mr. Wall is really kicking our butts
with all this, isn't he?

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.660
His face is cute, though.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.540
I've realized he's got
quite the disquieting vibe about him.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:50.330
I know what you mean!
Innocent, but scary, right?

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.160
Hold on. This is pretty amazing, right?

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.620
"Monday" mostly has articles
about pinup girls, right?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.410
It does feel like this has been in talks
for a while, even though it's sudden.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:01.830
It does feel like some nameless force
has been at work in all of this, for real.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.080
If anything, it's scary how real this feels.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.580
It's like an evil organization! Cool!

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:12.450
Gouda told us before, didn't he?
That we were all chosen.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:16.200
If we're to be so blessed with riches,
we should drink as deeply as possible.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.330
Who made you queen?

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.700
Well, there's no point in thinking about it.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:27.500
She's less like Nicole,
more like Queen Elizabeth?

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.450
This certainly got out of hand real quick.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.040
Cherry blossoms?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.200
Yes. You see, back in Japan, where I'm from,

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.830
this time of year,
all of the trees burst into bloom with them.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:54.000
I love their color and their scent.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.950
Is that where we get our names from?

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.950
I love that my name is Sakura!

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.450
I'm sorry. Are you okay?

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:07.910
I-I'm fine!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.660
And here we are.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.620
These are...

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.250
Cherry blossoms?

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:40.870
They're so cute!

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:47.950
These flowers bloom once a year,
usually around now.

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:54.660
They withstand the cold and bloom,
but they fall once it begins to rain.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:08:01.290
But that gentility makes them
more beautiful and sweet.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.290
They smell nice.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.870
Grandma! Grandma!

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:17.000
Let's go see the flowers again today!

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.620
Oh, my.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.120
Aren't I heavy?

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.290
It's okay! I'm like Iron Man!

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.410
That looks so yummy!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:34.660
It seems like we're on just a regular trip,
and it's been so much fun so far!

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.790
And it looks like the staff
is setting everything up for us, too.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:41.080
At this rate, we should make it there
by around noon.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:45.500
I'd love to go see the cherry blossoms
at Mount Yoshino, personally.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.950
"WEEKLY SHONEN MONDAY
PHOTO SHOOT SCHEDULE"

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.700
Hey, what do "Monday's"
circulation numbers look like?

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.540
What, getting scared?

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:55.200
No, not really.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.750
It looks like their numbers
are 300,000 units per week.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:00.120
They have it at the convenience store
and stuff, right?

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.660
Of course they do.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:10.250
What's up?

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.700
Nothing. It's amazing, right?
Getting a cover.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.200
The cherry blossoms
are in bloom in this region.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.790
The blooms at Mount Yoshino
will be even more amazing, I think.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.830
I wanna go see them soon!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.830
I-I'm looking forward to it.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.290
Interesting. You've been
staring at your own lunch all morning.

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.700
Hitome Senbon?

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.750
Yes, it's called Hitome Senbonzakura.

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:38.450
It's a place where you can see
lots of cherry blossoms at once.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.040
Really? That's amazing!

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:42.950
That's so cool, Grandma!
I want to go see them myself!

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:45.250
I have to see them! I have to!

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:57.040
I think that cherry blossoms
have a mysterious power to them.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:01.200
Such lovely blossoms
wrapped in such a beautiful scent.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:06.830
Just being around them for a little while
will make you forget all of your worries.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:11.120
I know what you mean!
Whenever I'm surrounded by their scent,

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:15.000
I feel happier and more energetic,
like I can do anything!

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.040
So I guess in that way,
you do the same thing for me, Grandma.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.160
Whenever I'm around you,
Grandma, I feel happier,

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:25.080
and I feel like I don't need
anyone but you around me.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.700
Oh, my. I wouldn't tell your parents that.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.700
I don't care what they think!

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:34.450
They've been too busy
with their work my entire life.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:38.750
Grandma Sakura,
you'll be by my side forever, won't you?

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.620
Hitome Senbonzakura.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:51.040
Why in the world
did the Wall send us here?

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:55.200
S-Sakura.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.580
Sorry. What's up?

00:10:57.580 --> 00:11:00.040
Um, well...

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:05.120
Due to an inspection, we'll be
stopping at Nagoya Station for a bit.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:08.370
We apologize for the inconvenience.

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:09.910
A delay, huh?

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:09.910
Please continue to wait
until this car resumes service.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.450
If only they'd told us when we left.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.200
But the deer are waiting for us!

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.200
Are we there yet?

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.500
We have another kilometer to go, they said.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:35.000
I'm pooped! I can't climb another step!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.250
The deer! Where are the deer?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.950
Toda, Nara isn't a breeding facility for deer.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:45.750
First the train, then the car stalled.
What the heck is going on?

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:49.370
The staff are carrying all of our luggage,
so you shouldn't complain.

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.000
Hey...

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.120
Aren't we really late?

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:57.790
Are we going to make the cover shoot at all?

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.500
We're here!

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.500
I'm pumped up!
Alright, it's time to shoot!

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:23.660
We really are surrounded
by cherry blossoms.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:27.790
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine, ten...

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:32.750
Toda, you might have more luck counting
if you go to that viewing platform over there.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:32.750
Eleven, twelve, thirteen, fourteen, fifteen,
sixteen seventeen, eighteen, nineteen, twenty...

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.330
Sakura?

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.500
This...

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.200
...is what Grandma...

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:09.000
Rain...

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:14.500
Sakura! Sakura!

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.370
Your grandmother's taken a fall.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.910
Oh my, Sakura.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.250
Grandma, you dummy!

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.870
Do you have any idea of how worried I was?

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:43.750
When Dad said you'd fallen, I...

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:46.750
I'm so sorry, Sakura.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:49.750
Are you sick or hurt anywhere?

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:52.160
I'm fine.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.660
Now let me see that pretty smile of yours.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:57.830
Okay!

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:05.620
Grandma, listen to this!

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:07.250
Oh, hello, Sakura.

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:09.700
The cherry blossoms were prettier than usual.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:13.410
I counted the ones on the right side,
and there were 300 of them!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.540
300 cherry blossoms! Isn't that amazing?

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.250
My, that is very amazing indeed!

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:23.700
I'm praying for you every day,
by that same cherry blossom tree.

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:27.620
Every day, I pray for your swift recovery.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:30.120
And I know you will get better really soon,

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:33.700
because that tree will surely listen
and grant my wish!

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.370
I really want to go see them with you.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:42.500
I see. Let's go see them together one day.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:43.910
It's a promise!

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:47.540
It's a promise.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:47.330
Grandma!

00:15:54.160 --> 00:16:00.830
I'm sorry that I couldn't fulfill
my end of our bargain.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.370
What are you saying?!

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:04.700
Don't say...

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.370
Don't say that!

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:13.370
Smile, Sakura...

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:20.790
I so dearly love that smile of yours.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:23.370
In your favorite places...

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:27.540
I'll make sure that the cherry blossoms
bloom for you always.

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.830
I'm here!

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:38.120
Even if the cherry blossoms start to fall,
I still have your name! And I'll still be here!

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:42.450
As long as I'm still here,
you'll be okay, Grandma.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.250
That's right.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.500
It just won't let up!

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:38.120
Who's the Rain Woman here?

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.700
It might be me.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.410
But children are always sunshine.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:42.580
How did you know?

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.080
By your smile, silly girl.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.950
Oh, are you praising me?

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:47.950
Hey, wait! Don't call me a child!

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:50.790
Quite frankly, it's useless to debate
about whether or not

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:54.700
unscientific things like Rain Women
and Sun Women even exist.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.290
Even though we finally got here
by sunset and everything...

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.790
We might not be able
to fulfill that Order now.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:02.540
With all of this rain, the blossoms will fall.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:05.160
Reshooting is going to be such a pain.

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:07.910
Guys!

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.410
Guys!

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:16.370
Let's take a picture!

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:18.950
Hey, you're totally soaked!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.160
You looked at cherry blossoms all this time?

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.660
Your phone's gonna get drenched.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:23.950
Anyone have a towel?

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:25.500
Makeup! Touch-up!

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:33.750
Just the fact I was able to come here at all
has made me so very happy.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.290
Someone take a picture
so we can remember this!

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:44.370
A picture of us
with thousands of blooms all in one place.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:49.870
Mew-Mew!

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.410
Beautiful.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:59.620
Your smile, Sakura. It's so beautiful.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:12.410
Thank you, Miu!

00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:15.290
No fair! I wanna take one, too!

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:18.330
Well, since the shoot itself
is pretty much a bust,

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:21.450
we may as well just grin and bear it.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.790
Cherry blossoms in the rain are nice, too.

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.290
Oh, for the love of...

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:27.200
Well, whatever.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:30.160
Everyone, wait!

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.750
Ah, Nicole, you're soaked!

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:38.040
Hey, get the camera ready.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:42.080
Get the rain covers up!
We're resuming the shoot!

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.500
Roger!

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:10.910
Smiles really are beautiful.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:12.950
What? In Japan?

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:14.580
What are you saying?

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.700
--Of course we're not okay with--
--Please!

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:18.040
Sakura...

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:21.750
Your mother and I are very busy.
And if you're alone in a foreign country...

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:24.540
It isn't a foreign country!

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:26.750
It's where Grandma is from!

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:29.370
And her blood runs in me, doesn't it?

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:33.410
When you think about that, does it really
seem strange that I would want to go there?

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:37.500
I know I'm being really selfish right now.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:41.830
If you let me do this, I promise
I'll never ask anything else of you.

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:43.500
I want to see them so badly!

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:47.080
Her homeland and
the cherry blossoms she loved!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.870
So please.

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:54.250
Please.

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:55.620
But that's...

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:57.830
I understand, Sakura.

00:20:57.830 --> 00:20:59.700
Dear...

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:02.370
But on one condition.

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:07.120
Here they are!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:08.790
So cool!

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:11.410
Wow, they actually came out pretty well.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.200
Our popularity has risen as a result.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.910
We'll top the yearly lists with this!

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:17.790
That's just unrealistic.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:19.950
W-Wow.

00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:26.250
All of us and the staff helped to create this,
and it became a book.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:29.120
Don't you think that's amazing?

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:37.160
Well, then, let's go to our lessons
with our heads held high, ladies!

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:38.610
Now that gets me in the mood!

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:39.040
Yep!

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.200
Don't get so in the mood
you trip over yourselves.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.110
Yeah, you're gonna fall!

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:43.950
No, I won't!

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:47.000
"DEADLINE IS ONE YEAR"'

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.200
Ah, Sakura. Are you okay?

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.040
Did something happen?

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.250
No.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:58.330
Let's go!

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.450
Okay.

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:33.160
"WEEKLY SHONEN MONDAY MAGAZINE"

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:39.080
Um, have I gotten any phone calls recently?

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.000
Phone calls?

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:43.950
We do get messages for you guys
from the fans cheering you on.

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:46.870
Oh, um, not those.

00:23:46.870 --> 00:23:48.750
You're acting awfully strange, Kono.

00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:50.910
Oh, he smiled. Scary.

00:23:50.910 --> 00:23:52.580
Never mind!

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:58.910
--Man, that's hilarious, but it's so true.
--Right?

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:12.000
"Episode 5: Just Flip It Over!"

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:12.000
"Just Flip It Over!"
